; Matching is on the value's parsed `(magnitude, unit)` pair, not on its
; text. Two reasons: the binary walker has no source text to compare
; against, so a text rule could not be dual-path at all — and the pair is
; the better rule anyway, since it decides these four cases correctly with
; no special-casing.
;
;   * `2d`   — matches.
;   * `2.0d` — matches. Same magnitude, same unit.
;   * `02d`  — matches. The leading zero is not part of the identity.
;   * `2`    — does NOT match: no unit, so it is not a spelling at all.
;              `wrong_underlying`, exactly as before this feature existed.
;   * `2.5d` — does NOT match: a fractional magnitude is not an integer
;              key, so it cannot round into `2d`.
(plugin :name gpu :version "1.0.0" :sjon "1.3"
  (value-kind :name texture-dimension :underlying symbol
    :members (member-set :values [1d 2d 3d]))
  (form :name texture (key :name dimension :type texture-dimension)))

(texture :dimension 2d)
(texture :dimension 2.0d)
(texture :dimension 02d)
(texture :dimension 2)
(texture :dimension 2.5d)
